And I'll just show
the second video,

00:21:29.699 --> 00:21:31.240
which I'm going to
have trouble with,

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:32.710
which is why I'm
skipping a slide.

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:35.090
So this is the
last video I have.

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:37.610
And let me see if I
can do this by clicking

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.680
on the right-hand side here.

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:41.950
Let's see if this just works.

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:43.680
Ha, it works.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:50.220
So with PBS works we actually
let you build an appliance

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:51.570
on the Cloud with a few clicks.

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:54.420
So this is the interface
inside of PBScloud.io,

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:57.090
which is the software as a
service version of PBS Control.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:22:00.570
You just say, hey, I want
to build an appliance.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.640
Say a few things
about what you want.

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:07.170
You pick Google compute
platform, because we're here.

00:22:07.170 --> 00:22:09.990
You can pick the region
where you want to run.

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:12.250
And then, actually, for the
appliance, in this case,

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:15.460
we're building a
HyperWorks appliance.

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:18.540
You'll actually pick the kinds
of instances you want in here.

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:20.410
I'm actually picking
a 96 CPU instance,

00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:22.770
so that will get me Skylake.

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:26.190
We automatically
fill in for you all

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:30.477
of this crazy stuff you
need in order to actually do

00:22:30.477 --> 00:22:31.560
this administration stuff.

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:33.643
You can, of course, change
it because you have to.

00:22:33.643 --> 00:22:34.980
And that's it.

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:38.550
The beautiful interface I showed
you on the Windows desktop

00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:41.970
also is available
as a web interface.

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:46.192
It's just as beautiful
but maybe not as simple.

00:22:46.192 --> 00:22:48.150
But if you want to submit
a job through the web

00:22:48.150 --> 00:22:51.154
instead of through the desktop,
more or less the same thing.

00:22:51.154 --> 00:22:52.570
You pick the
application you want.

00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:54.810
You say, here's the file I want.

00:22:54.810 --> 00:23:02.190
Fill in anything
that's not defaulted.

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:03.817
And click Submit.

00:23:03.817 --> 00:23:05.400
You can actually get
a lot more access

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:08.746
through the web about what's
happening if you need to.

00:23:08.746 --> 00:23:10.620
So you can actually find
out what's going on.

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:13.380
You can check the files
as they're running

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:14.610
on supercomputing center.

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:15.690
You can check the
files, actually,

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:17.565
if you burst into the
cloud, you can actually

00:23:17.565 --> 00:23:21.330
see the files of the running
job while it's there.

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:23.730
You can get all sorts
of job attributes.

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:25.470
Perhaps one of the
very neat things

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.020
that you can do through
this interface--

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:29.700
I don't have my timing perfect--

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.790
is you can also do remote
visualization, which

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:34.800
means you can take
something like a Chromebook

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:39.720
here with no memory and you can
submit a job, a graphics job,

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:43.350
that's going to use, say,
256 gigabytes of memory

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:45.660
and all sorts of
huge, powerful stuff.

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:48.260
And you can say, please
run this job in the Cloud,

00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:53.100
but I want you to stream
the bits back in my browser

00:23:53.100 --> 00:23:56.070
so that I can actually do the
work no matter where I am.

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:58.159
And it's as simple as,
while I was talking,

00:23:58.159 --> 00:23:58.950
what you saw there.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:00.120
You just say, here's
what I want to run.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:00.960
I want to run on the Cloud.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:02.876
We do all the orchestration
behind the scenes.

00:24:02.876 --> 00:24:03.990
We set everything up.

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:06.840
And you can run huge and
fantastic large-- yeah,

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:09.660
sorry about that, bicyclist--

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:12.960
fantastic, large
simulations, even

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:15.730
from a really small device.

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:17.900
And with that, I'm
going to turn it over

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:22.370
to the next speaker, Peter.

00:24:22.370 --> 00:24:23.694
Thank you.

